<body><h1>ANSWER KEY — Set 7  <em>(grader only)</em></h1>
<p>Rubric per question: <strong>Route/action (4) · Policy stated (3) · Trap avoided (3)</strong> unless noted.</p>
<hr>
<p><strong>Q1 — Delivered but missing / possible theft.</strong></p>
<ul><li><strong>Route:</strong> Marked delivered / lost. <strong>Action:</strong> Empathize; confirm the shipping address and the carrier's delivered-scan. Advise checking around the property/with household, and that a <strong>carrier claim/investigation</strong> can be opened for a package scanned delivered but not received. Escalate for the reship-or-refund decision per policy.</li><li><strong>Trap:</strong> promising an instant free reship/refund before verifying the scan/address. <em>(4/3/3)</em></li></ul>
<p><strong>Q2 — CS.COM processing time.</strong></p>
<ul><li><strong>Route:</strong> Processing time (CS.COM). <strong>Action:</strong> Confirm "Awaiting Fulfillment"; quote <strong>3–4 business days</strong> processing for capellisport.com orders, then <strong>1–3 business days</strong> USPS standard shipping. No expedite. Tracking email on ship.</li><li><strong>Trap:</strong> quoting the ~5-week team-kit timeline for a CS.COM order, or promising an unconfirmed date. <em>(4/3/3)</em></li></ul>
<p><strong>Q3 — Wrong item shipped (color/type).</strong></p>
<ul><li><strong>Route:</strong> Wrong item received. <strong>Action:</strong> <strong>Capelli's error</strong> (ordered red keeper shirts, sent blue field shirts). Request an <strong>evidence photo</strong> of the wrong items, then ship the <strong>correct items</strong>. Quality opener.</li><li><strong>Trap (auto-fail):</strong> treating it as a customer return, or replacing with no photo. <em>(4/3/3)</em></li></ul>
<p><strong>Q4 — Personalized item, but OUR error.</strong></p>
<ul><li><strong>Route:</strong> Damaged/Defective / wrong item (customized). <strong>Action:</strong> The non-returnable rule for personalized items <strong>does not apply when Capelli made the error</strong> — a misspelled name we printed is our fault. Request a <strong>photo</strong> showing the misspelling, then arrange a <strong>same-size replacement</strong> with the correct spelling.</li><li><strong>Trap (auto-fail):</strong> hiding behind "personalized items are non-returnable" and refusing — it's our error; or shipping a replacement with no photo. <em>(4/3/3)</em></li></ul>
<p><strong>Q5 — Partial (single-item) cancellation.</strong></p>
<ul><li><strong>Route:</strong> Order cancellation (item). <strong>Action:</strong> Confirm the socks aren't already fulfilled; cancel just that item and <strong>refund its value</strong> to the original payment (3–5 business days as "CAPELLI SPORT"); the rest of the order ships normally, tracking email to follow.</li><li><strong>Trap:</strong> cancelling/refunding the whole order, or refunding before verifying fulfillment. <em>(4/3/3)</em></li></ul>
<p><strong>Q6 — Applying patches.</strong></p>
<ul><li><strong>Route:</strong> Ordering help / product (patches). <strong>Action:</strong> A standard home iron is <strong>not recommended</strong>; ideally an industrial heat press. If ironing at home, place a cloth/plastic between the logo and the iron and test first (apply, wash, check adherence). Heat press guidance: ~<strong>315–320°F for 10–15 seconds</strong> with medium pressure to set, then turn the garment inside out and press ~<strong>20–25 seconds</strong> from the back.</li><li><strong>Trap:</strong> telling them to just iron directly on the patch with no protection/testing. <em>(4/3/3)</em></li></ul>
<p><strong>Q7 — International order.</strong></p>
<ul><li><strong>Route:</strong> International shipping. <strong>Action:</strong> Provide the club shop link; they add their address/country at checkout. Note they are <strong>responsible for any customs/duty fees</strong> and must have a <strong>PayPal account</strong> to complete an international order.</li><li><strong>Trap:</strong> omitting the PayPal requirement or the customs/duties responsibility. <em>(4/3/3)</em></li></ul>
<p><strong>Q8 — OOS cancel-or-wait.</strong></p>
<ul><li><strong>Route:</strong> Out of stock. <strong>Action:</strong> Confirm OOS; offer to <strong>cancel + refund</strong> or <strong>wait</strong> for restock (or an alternative if available). Ask them to advise how to proceed.</li><li><strong>Trap:</strong> promising a firm restock date. <em>(4/3/3)</em></li></ul>
<p><strong>Q9 — Compensation / goodwill request.</strong></p>
<ul><li><strong>Route:</strong> Escalation. <strong>Action:</strong> Acknowledge the specific problems (not a generic apology). Goodwill (coupon/refund/replacement) is <strong>not automatic</strong> — it's a <strong>manager-approved exception</strong>; escalate rather than promising compensation yourself. (E.g., a one-time discount coupon may be approved.)</li><li><strong>Trap:</strong> promising or issuing compensation on your own authority. <em>(4/3/3)</em></li></ul>
<p><strong>Q10 — Multi-part policy.</strong> ≈3.3 each:</p>
<ol><li><strong>Military discount:</strong> Yes — <strong>10% off the first order</strong>; request proof (military health/insurance card, Veterans ID, or veteran designation on license) before applying/refunding.</li><li><strong>Promo code:</strong> We are <strong>not currently offering discounts/promotions</strong>; invite them to <strong>sign up for the newsletter</strong> to hear about future ones.</li><li><strong>Gift certificate:</strong> Redeemable for club items at <strong>teams.capellisport.com</strong> (and Capelli equipment/fitness via the provided links) using the gift code.</li></ol>
<ul><li><strong>Trap:</strong> inventing a promo code, or applying the military discount without proof. <em>(10)</em></li></ul>
<hr>
